        "index": 1,
        "start": 0,
        "end": 13.76,
        "text": "What if an indicator could open a whole new perspective? Step through the digital looking glass. Meet Pivotglass: a workspace for asking better questions, following evidence, and seeing an investigation take shape."
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "start": 13.76,
        "end": 29.12,
        "text": "Start with a question, an indicator, or a report. Guided coaching helps new analysts get moving. Preview local documents, choose what to admit, and open complete source details. Every step gives you something you can inspect."
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "start": 29.12,
        "end": 43.04,
        "text": "Then change your perspective. Follow typed relationships. Reconstruct provenance and analyst groups. Scan the constellation for uneven coverage. A crowded case becomes a set of questions you can actually work."
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "start": 43.04,
        "end": 59.36,
        "text": "Twelve evidence views reveal different sides of the same workspace: stored types, Dossier completeness, investigation and enrichment activity, connection counts, and coverage similarity. The view explains its question and exposes its exact data."
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "start": 59.36,
        "end": 79.04,
        "text": "Compare competing hypotheses. Explore the investigation hierarchy. Keep likelihood separate from confidence. Structured techniques make assumptions, contradictions, and next collection needs visible. Then turn the work into a reviewable report, saved as Markdown or printed to PDF."
      },
      {
        "index": 6,
        "start": 79.04,
        "end": 99.6,
        "text": "Choose your atmosphere, including original generative music. Begin locally with the synthetic quickstart, then enable services deliberately. Download Pivotglass from github dot com slash jarocki slash pivotglass. Follow a connection. Ask a sharper question. Discover what the evidence can show."
      }
