        "index": 1,
        "start": 0,
        "end": 18.32,
        "text": "A file. A domain. An address. On their own, they are fragments. Pivotglass helps you follow the thread between them. This is a synthetic, offline case: the relationships are already stored, so we can explore without pretending to query a live intelligence service."
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "start": 18.32,
        "end": 34.48,
        "text": "Start with invoice viewer dot bin. Its recorded relationship points to beacon check dot example. Open the domain and inspect the basis. That first pivot changes the question: what infrastructure did the file touch, and when was the connection observed?"
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "start": 34.48,
        "end": 52.56,
        "text": "From the domain, follow resolves to the address, then hosts to the URL. Each edge has a type. Open details at each stop instead of treating a line as proof. Now a single file has led us to an infrastructure neighborhood and a more specific collection plan."
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "start": 52.56,
        "end": 67.52,
        "text": "Provenance tells you where the records came from. The chronological trail records how material entered the investigation. These are reviewable paths, not an automatically reconstructed attack chain. A missing event remains missing."
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "start": 67.52,
        "end": 84.8,
        "text": "Two admitted indicators also share an analyst promotion group. The dotted edges preserve why we selected them together. That is workflow context, not evidence of one owner. Read the complete wrapped URL, filter the neighborhood, and keep the distinctions visible."
      },
      {
        "index": 6,
        "start": 84.8,
        "end": 103.44,
        "text": "The useful result is a better test. Does this topology fit common control, shared hosting, or both? Record a rationale, identify independent evidence that could separate them, and choose the next authorized collection. Pivotglass turns a connection into a question you can investigate."
      }
    ],
